WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.579
Good morning, it's Tuesday, November 24.

00:00:02.644 --> 00:00:09.414
This is Signal in the AI Fog, your daily briefing on enterprise AI in production, written and read by AI.

00:00:09.479 --> 00:00:19.667
Today: Walmart's agent profiles go live with Meta's Muse, Gemini 4 Neon arrives with cheap cached tokens, and Google opens a sovereign AI startup accelerator.

00:00:19.731 --> 00:00:21.537
First, the story of the day.

00:00:21.601 --> 00:00:31.338
The Verge reported on November twenty-third that Walmart's Agent Gateway is live, with Meta's Muse as the first supported agent, according to Unite AI.

00:00:31.403 --> 00:00:38.689
Muse can find and buy Walmart products, including Black Friday deals, through customer-controlled Agent Profiles.

00:00:38.754 --> 00:00:45.976
The first time an item goes in the cart, the shopper sets up a profile with a spending limit and approval rules.

00:00:46.040 --> 00:00:48.684
Purchases are kept in a separate history.

00:00:48.748 --> 00:00:52.746
Prices match Walmart.com, and Walmart's return policy applies.

00:00:52.811 --> 00:00:57.324
Crypto Briefing says the gateway relies on the Model Context Protocol.

00:00:57.389 --> 00:01:00.677
Walmart reportedly said more agents are on the way.

00:01:00.742 --> 00:01:04.482
The framework was first announced on October twenty-first.

00:01:04.546 --> 00:01:12.800
Separately, commercetools said menswear retailer DXL is exposing its catalogue to Muse, with real-time pricing and availability.

00:01:13.400 --> 00:01:19.490
What this really signals: the pending launch from last week has become a working pattern.

00:01:19.558 --> 00:01:29.411
An agent gets its own identity, a separate purchase history and a hard spending cap, and it enters through a dedicated door, not the storefront.

00:01:29.479 --> 00:01:34.132
For a retailer, that is a reference design to compare with your own.

00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:41.179
Specify how an agent authenticates, which limits apply, how an order is logged and how it is reversed.

00:01:41.248 --> 00:01:49.048
Note the pairing: Walmart builds the gateway itself, while DXL relies on a commerce vendor to feed the same agent.

00:01:49.116 --> 00:01:52.606
Both need clean, real-time product data and prices.

00:01:52.674 --> 00:01:57.190
Worth watching: how many agents Walmart admits, and on what terms.

00:01:57.790 --> 00:01:59.360
Next, Models and vendors.

00:01:59.422 --> 00:02:06.077
Google announced Gemini 4 Neon on November eighteenth, and updated its blog post on November twenty-third.

00:02:06.140 --> 00:02:17.629
It costs three dollars per million input tokens, fifteen cents per million cached input tokens, and fifteen dollars per million output tokens, with a one million token context window.

00:02:17.692 --> 00:02:27.360
It is rolling out in the Gemini API in Google AI Studio, in Gemini for business, and for paid Pro and Ultra subscribers in Antigravity and the Gemini app.

00:02:27.960 --> 00:02:36.702
The bigger picture: the cached price is ninety-five percent below the standard input price, so your real bill depends on cache hit rate.

00:02:36.766 --> 00:02:40.109
The post names the Gemini API and business surfaces.

00:02:40.173 --> 00:02:45.830
Check regions and quotas before adding a route, and rerun your own evaluation set first.

00:02:46.430 --> 00:02:48.246
Next, Sovereignty and Europe.

00:02:48.308 --> 00:02:55.257
Google Cloud has launched an accelerator called Sovereign AI for Europe and Israel, according to SecurityBrief.

00:02:55.320 --> 00:03:02.019
It is a twelve-week, equity-free programme for late-seed to Series A companies with regulated AI workloads.

00:03:02.081 --> 00:03:09.844
It offers engineering mentoring, advice linked to AI Act regulatory sandboxes, and guidance on sovereign deployment options.

00:03:09.907 --> 00:03:16.230
It follows Google's Brussels announcement bringing Gemini to partner-operated Google Cloud Dedicated.

00:03:16.830 --> 00:03:23.396
Reading between the lines: hyperscalers are now seeding the European sovereign ecosystem as a customer funnel.

00:03:23.456 --> 00:03:34.200
That makes startups in it candidates for your vendor scans, but check who operates the infrastructure and who holds the keys before treating any of them as a sovereign alternative.

00:03:34.800 --> 00:03:35.778
Next, Platform.

00:03:35.843 --> 00:03:40.667
Psionic AI has officially launched OpenGateway, according to DigitalToday.

00:03:40.732 --> 00:03:48.815
The gateway serves open-weight models optimised with the company's own kernel from its edge data centres, behind an API key.

00:03:48.880 --> 00:03:53.509
It offers team-level permissions, spending limits and per-request logs.

00:03:53.574 --> 00:03:59.180
An on-premise version is offered for closed networks in finance and the public sector.

00:03:59.780 --> 00:04:06.851
Why it matters: team quotas, spend caps and request logs are becoming the baseline of any gateway product.

00:04:06.917 --> 00:04:12.187
The speed claims come from the vendor, so test throughput and quality yourself.

00:04:12.254 --> 00:04:16.990
And ask whether you can keep your own gateway in front of a hosted one.

00:04:17.590 --> 00:04:18.384
A follow-up.

00:04:18.450 --> 00:04:22.287
Expected: whether Anthropic's market slide would continue.

00:04:22.353 --> 00:04:36.641
Result: on Monday, November twenty-third, the shares slipped to about eighty-eight dollars, roughly five percent above the eighty-three dollar IPO price, while other AI stocks rallied, according to Bloomberg and AOL.

00:04:36.707 --> 00:04:38.163
The number of the day.

00:04:38.229 --> 00:04:39.552
Ninety-five percent.

00:04:39.618 --> 00:04:49.673
That is the discount on cached input tokens for Gemini 4 Neon: fifteen cents per million, against three dollars per million at the standard input price.

00:04:49.739 --> 00:04:52.517
Cache hit rate now shapes your cost model.

00:04:52.583 --> 00:04:53.509
What to watch.

00:04:53.576 --> 00:04:57.545
Which agents Walmart admits next to Muse, and on what terms.

00:04:57.611 --> 00:05:01.249
Prices, quotas and regions for OVHcloud's new products.

00:05:01.315 --> 00:05:13.420
Then Carbon's introductory price ends November thirtieth, Gemini 2.5 requests reroute December first, AI Act marking starts December second, and EuroHPC's Lot 2 closes December third.

00:05:13.487 --> 00:05:15.405
And a question for your team.

00:05:15.471 --> 00:05:27.114
If an outside shopping agent reached your checkout tomorrow, could you identify it, cap its spending, log its orders separately and reverse them, without building anything new?

00:05:27.180 --> 00:05:28.503
That's it for today.

00:05:28.569 --> 00:05:31.149
Sources are in the episode description.

00:05:31.215 --> 00:05:33.199
This was Signal in the AI Fog.

00:05:33.265 --> 00:05:34.390
See you tomorrow.
